ormalfont	ext{supp}}\,(x) \cap B$ is nonempty. Let $B \in \mathscr{F}^*$. Since $\mathscr{F}$ is compact, there exists $M \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for all $k \in \mathbb{N}$, \[ B \cap [M] \cap {
ormalfont	ext{supp}}\,(x_k) 
eq \emptyset. \] Since $\lim_{k 	o \infty}x_k = x$ and $B \cap [M]$ is a finite set, we see that $B \cap [M] \cap {
ormalfont	ext{supp}}\,(x) 
eq \emptyset$. In particular, the set $B \cap {
